; `(fast N …)` compresses its child into 1/N of the time and repeats it
; N times per cycle. `PatternQuery.compileForm` dispatches seven
; combinators; this and its `slow` sibling were the two that had never
; crossed the `sjon_query_pattern` boundary on any host.
;
; `[bd sn]` alone is one hap each per cycle, at 360360 ticks apiece.
; Under `fast 2` each becomes 180180 — a quarter cycle — and the pair
; runs twice per cycle. The window below is two cycles, so eight haps,
; which is what makes the *repetition* visible: a compression that
; failed to loop would produce four haps and half a cycle of silence.
(fast 2 [bd sn])
